# Sprint 20 — Windows Authentication Detection Engineering

**Status:** Complete 
**Detection:** DET-002 — Repeated Failed Authentication Detection 
**MITRE ATT&CK:** T1110 — Brute Force 
**Primary Data Source:** Windows Security Event Log 
**Primary Event ID:** 4625 — An account failed to log on 
**SIEM:** Splunk Enterprise

---

## Objective

Develop and validate a behavioral detection for repeated Windows authentication failures using existing Windows Security telemetry collected by Splunk.

Sprint 20 expanded the SOC lab beyond network-based detection by introducing identity and authentication monitoring.

The sprint focused on:

- Validating domain connectivity
- Verifying Windows Security telemetry
- Analyzing Event ID 4625
- Generating controlled failed authentication attempts
- Developing DET-002
- Identifying the correct username field
- Establishing a behavioral threshold
- Performing positive and negative validation
- Operationalizing DET-002 as a scheduled Splunk alert
- Mapping the detection to MITRE ATT&CK T1110
- Developing an analyst triage workflow
- Documenting false-positive and tuning considerations

