## Analyst Response

When DET-002 triggers, the analyst should:

1. Identify the affected `TargetUserName`.
2. Determine the number and frequency of failed attempts.
3. Identify the source host or IP when available.
4. Review the logon type.
5. Review the failure reason.
6. Determine whether multiple accounts were targeted.
7. Search for successful authentication following the failures.
8. Review additional activity from the source.
9. Determine whether the activity has a legitimate explanation.
10. Escalate unexplained or suspicious authentication activity.

Investigation workflow:

```text
DET-002 Triggered
        |
        v
Identify Account
        |
        v
Identify Source
        |
        v
Review Failure Count
        |
        v
Review Logon Type
        |
        v
Search for Event 4624
        |
        v
Check Related Activity
        |
        v
Determine Context
        |
        +----------------------+
        |                      |
        v                      v
    Authorized             Suspicious
        |                      |
        v                      v
 Document / Close       Investigate / Escalate
```

