## False Positive Considerations

Repeated authentication failures can occur for many legitimate reasons.

Potential false positives include:

- User password mistakes
- Recently changed passwords
- Cached credentials
- Mapped drives using old credentials
- Services using stale passwords
- Scheduled tasks using outdated credentials
- Application authentication failures
- Administrator troubleshooting
- Authorized penetration testing

Production implementation would require environmental baselining and tuning.

Potential tuning strategies include:

```text
Baseline Normal Failures
        |
        v
Identify Noisy Accounts
        |
        v
Identify Service Accounts
        |
        v
Tune Failure Threshold
        |
        v
Tune Time Window
        |
        v
Evaluate Source Systems
        |
        v
Consider Account Sensitivity
        |
        v
Correlate Successful Logons
```

The current threshold of five failures within five minutes was selected specifically for the controlled lab environment.

